 `ReplicatedStorage.MarketReign.ChartViewportTests` checks time/price panning, retained-history bounds, anchored zoom, live-update isolation, Go live, mobile geometry and single-candle behavior. Mouse gestures, wheel zoom, return to live, and drawing movement were additionally exercised in Studio Play mode.
 
+## Owner bot accounting refresh
+
+The server-only `/bots refresh` command uses the same creator/group-owner authorization as `/reset` and `/give`. It accepts exactly `refresh`, queues one request, and starts before the next simulation request batch. The saved exchange must be available; local unsaved worlds cannot acknowledge a durable reset. Duplicate callbacks are debounced, overlapping operations are rejected, and a monotonically increasing checkpoint receipt prevents replay of the same operation.
+
+Every participant bot receives the existing `BotPopulation.Capital[Kind]` allocation as its new equity, including retiring bots and bots in close-only markets. Players, clearing accounts and archives are excluded. The capital adjustment is allocation minus marked equity, so profitable bots may withdraw capital and negative-equity bots may require more than their allocation. No capital configuration, prices, candles, volume or execution records change.
+
+Each bot records the adjustment, actor, sequence, simulation step, prior realized/unrealized P&L and cash change in `CapitalAdjustments`. `Base = StartingCapital + NetCapitalAdjustments` continues to mean contributed capital. `PnlBaseline` retains prior economic P&L; `Balance = Base + PnlBaseline + Realized`. Current reported P&L is `Realized + Unrealized`, also returned as `Summary.Session`. Open positions retain their strategy/execution `Entry` and gain an accounting-only `PnlEntry` at the refresh mark. Partial closes and scale-ins use that independent cost basis; reversals start a new basis. Consequently a close at the refresh mark earns zero even when the original entry differed. Trade history remains historical evidence, with new closing rows carrying the accounting entry when applicable.
+
+`World:RefreshBots` prepares and audits detached accounting records, encodes the complete checkpoint, and waits for the fenced lease commit before applying those records to the original in-memory bot objects. Simulation is paused during the transaction. Bot strategies, original positions, pending exits, retry deadlines, order objects and priorities remain intact; player accounts and requests are not replaced by an epoch swap. A single eligibility revision wakes existing retry controls when newly funded resting liquidity becomes executable. Save ambiguity pauses and reloads the durable result instead of guessing or executing again.
+
+Checkpoint V17 persists these baselines and the receipt; older engines fail closed. Do not resume a V17 world on an older build. `BotRefreshTests` covers long/short open gains and losses, partial entry/exit fills, scale-ins/reversals, negative equity, queued protections, all categories and retired obligations, owner rejection, repeated commands, scheduler boundaries, storage failure and lost acknowledgments. Validation uses detached fixtures and captured-state copies, never an active account. Installation must occur in Studio Edit mode; save the local place and start a new play session to load the updated modules. Subsequent refresh commands do not restart the simulation.
+
 ## Replay and validation
 
 Reproducibility is defined by seed, configuration, and the same account actions at the same simulation steps in the same order. Wall-clock delays are not replay coordinates. The central scheduler does not skip steps when catching up. `MarketTests` compares the complete execution tape between two seeded runs with identical step-indexed player actions and checks that another seed produces a different result.
